  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 248 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nThere is a consensus among ensemble and deterministic guidance\nthat once the ridge moves over the region tomorrow, that it will\nremain through the week. This leads to high confidence in a\nrelatively uneventful week. The ridge will be bookended by\ntroughing along the West and East Coasts causing weak low-level\nsouthwesterly flow during the week. As a result, there exists\nsupport for warm air advection, albeit subtly. This will result\nin a gradual warming of temperatures through the week. The first\nhalf of the week will see a return to near normal temperatures,\nbut how much we warm by the end of the week remains uncertain.\nLREF guidance has Thursday\u2019s high temperatures in the low to\nmid-70s, while the NBM has upper-70s to low-80s. The NBM is\nlikely warmer due to it being composed of bias-corrected\nguidance that is warmer than non-bias guidance. This warm bias\nis likely a result of it currently being the cooling season\ncombined with recent unseasonably warm events. Given this\npotential impact from the bias correction, the NBM is probably\ntoo warm and confidence is low in its temperatures towards the\nend of the week.\n\nConfidence is high in dry conditions prevailing through the week\ndue to the presence of weak flow aloft and lack of any notable\ndisturbances in both deterministic and ensemble guidance.",
